      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-26121",
      ":question/problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(4,-3)$ lies on the curve $y = f(x)$ and the point $Q$ with coordinates $(4, 3)$ lies on the curve $y = g(x)$. If the curve $y = g(x)$ is related to $y = f(x)$ via the transformation $g(x) = f(x) + k$, then what is the value of $k$?"
